{"step_index":1469,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-21T17:48:48Z","thinking":"**Implementing Touch Gestures**\n\nI'm currently integrating unified touch gesture handlers within `DialerHudScreen.tsx`. I've started by initializing `touchStartX` and `touchStartY` using `useRef` to manage the starting coordinates of touch events, which is foundational for enabling swipe recognition across both web and native environments.\n\n\n**Refining Gesture Detection**\n\nI've added `isSwipingHorizontally` to the `useRef` hooks in `DialerHudScreen.tsx` to precisely differentiate between vertical scrolling and horizontal swipes. The `onGestureMove` function now determines swipe dominance using `dx` and `dy`, canceling horizontal swipe attempts if vertical scrolling is detected. I am also determining swipe direction and setting the UI feedback to the user!\n\n\n**Finalizing Gesture Interactions**\n\nI've completed the gesture handling within `DialerHudScreen.tsx`.  The `onGestureEnd` function now executes different actions based on swipe direction: a right swipe dials and left swipes advances the lead. Haptic feedback is also added using `HapticsService` for a better user experience. Animation provides visual feedback, returning the UI to its initial position. The `panResponder.panHandlers` are set to handle touch gestures. I've also added the appropriate actions to cancel and reset appropriately.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add universal Web and Native swipe gesture engine to DialerHudScreen.tsx","EndLine":210,"Instruction":"Add universal gesture controllers","ReplacementContent":"  // Web & Native Universal Swipe Engine\n  const touchStartX = useRef<number | null>(null);\n  const touchStartY = useRef<number | null>(null);\n  const isSwipingHorizontally = useRef<boolean>(false);\n\n  const onGestureStart = (clientX: number, clientY: number) => {\n    touchStartX.current = clientX;\n    touchStartY.current = clientY;\n    isSwipingHorizontally.current = false;\n  };\n\n  const onGestureMove = (clientX: number, clientY: number) => {\n    if (touchStartX.current === null) return;\n    const dx = clientX - touchStartX.current;\n    const dy = clientY - (touchStartY.current || clientY);\n\n    if (!isSwipingHorizontally.current) {\n      if (Math.abs(dx) > 10 && Math.abs(dx) > Math.abs(dy)) {\n        isSwipingHorizontally.current = true;\n      } else if (Math.abs(dy) > 10) {\n        touchStartX.current = null;\n        return;\n      }\n    }\n\n    if (isSwipingHorizontally.current) {\n      pan.setValue({ x: dx, y: 0 });\n      if (dx > 50) {\n        setSwipeActionText('📞 RELEASE TO DIAL');\n      } else if (dx < -50) {\n        setSwipeActionText('⏭️ RELEASE TO SKIP');\n      } else {\n        setSwipeActionText(null);\n      }\n    }\n  };\n\n  const onGestureEnd = () => {\n    if (touchStartX.current === null) return;\n    const wasSwiping = isSwipingHorizontally.current;\n    touchStartX.current = null;\n    touchStartY.current = null;\n    isSwipingHorizontally.current = false;\n\n    if (!wasSwiping) return;\n\n    const currentX = (pan.x as any)._value || 0;\n\n    if (currentX > 50) {\n      HapticsService.medium();\n      handleDial();\n      Animated.timing(pan, {\n        toValue: { x: 350, y: 0 },\n        duration: 160,\n        useNativeDriver: false,\n      }).start(() => {\n        pan.setValue({ x: 0, y: 0 });\n        setSwipeActionText(null);\n      });\n    } else if (currentX < -50) {\n      HapticsService.tick();\n      advanceNextLead();\n      Animated.timing(pan, {\n        toValue: { x: -350, y: 0 },\n        duration: 160,\n        useNativeDriver: false,\n      }).start(() => {\n        pan.setValue({ x: 0, y: 0 });\n        setSwipeActionText(null);\n      });\n    } else {\n      Animated.spring(pan, {\n        toValue: { x: 0, y: 0 },\n        friction: 6,\n        tension: 50,\n        useNativeD