{"step_index":1500,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T19:19:10Z","content":"**Yes, automatically.** The app is designed with an **intelligent priority queue** that always remembers where you left off.\n\nHere is exactly how it works:\n\n---\n\n### 🧠 How the Queue Logic Resumes Your Dialing\n\n1. **Untouched Leads First (`attempts_count = 0`):**\n   - When you have 13 leads, all 13 start with `0 attempts`.\n   - When you call and disposition leads 1 through 7 (e.g., as *No Answer*, *Spoke*, *Appt. Set*, etc.), their attempt counts increase to `1`, and their statuses update in the database.\n   - Leads 8 through 13 still have `0 attempts`.\n\n2. **Automatic Resume at Lead 8:**\n   - When you stop and return later, the Power Dialer queries the database using:\n     ```sql\n     ORDER BY attempts_count ASC, created_at ASC\n     ```\n   - Because leads 8 through 13 have never been called (`0 attempts`), the app **automatically places Lead 8 at the very top of your queue** (showing *Educator 1 of 6 remaining* on your 1st round).\n\n3. **Closed Leads Are Removed:**\n   - If any of your previous calls resulted in **`🎯 Appt. Set`**, **`🚫 Do Not Call`**, or **`Disqualified`**, they are automatically moved out of the active dialing queue so you never waste time dialing them again.\n\n4. **Multi-Touch Cadence Rounds:**\n   - Once you finish calling leads 8 through 13 (completing Round 1 for all 13 contacts), the dialer will automatically queue up any *No Answer* contacts for **Call #2** according to your Cadence settings.","thinking":"**Analyzing Dialer Behavior**\n\nOkay, I'm examining the `DialerHudScreen.tsx` and `leadsRepository.ts` files. Specifically, I've noted how lead dispositions 1 through 7 affect the `attempts_count` and status updates. Also looking at the power dialer start function and how that affects lead data.\n\n\n"}
