{"step_index":1502,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T19:22:55Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 8 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. i think that once a lead pic is 'snapped' in, while it's processing, there should be some indicator...like a spinning indicator to let the user know the app hasnty crashed.  as it currently is, it does nothing until the processing is done...but that takes around 3-5sec.  what are your thoughts?\n2. there is a section in the main dashboard that tracks 'Sit-Downs'.  In concept that is good, however it should be more indicative of an appointment being set from the call...'Appointments Set'  there should be some way in the power dialer screen to disposition the call as 'Appt. Set' in addition to the other disposition options.  what are your thoughts?  my goal is to be able to used this app to not only keep all old and new lead data at the users finger tips, but to also track the most important KPIs as related to calling leads like these.\n3. it's now giving the error: Can't find variable BarChart3.  correct this and run a detailed check that there are no other uncaught bugs or errors\n4. for the power dialer HUD, the screen is extremely crowded....the dispo buttons overlap the dial/call button...whether in standard or landscape mode.  the ux/ui should unsure efficient and elegant use on any handheld device.\n5. now the swipe right to dial/swipe left to skip functionality doesn't seem fully functional/implemented.  please verify\n6. also, the 'Report Card Needs & Inquiries\" section in the HUD doesn't extend to multiple lines and instead runs off of the screen.  please elegantly address this utilizing best practices for ux/ui design\n7. ok...the swipe still does not trigger a dial when swiped right.  i only have one test record so i'm not sure if the swipe left to skip is actually working, but swipe right is not.  my understanding is that swiping right should trigger the same behavior as if the Dial # button was clicked.\n8. just tested the new build.   the swipe functionality still isn't working\n9. does the app automatically keep track of where a user left off in their dialing...for example, if i have 13 leads, and i start calling but have to stop after call 7, does the app pick up on lead 8 when i start it back up?\n10. how does it handle it when new leads are added?  does it just append them to the end or does it reset the dial count?\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n# Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Explain How New Leads Are Handled In Queue Ordering:**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"how does it handle it when new leads are added? does it just append them to the end or does it reset the dial count?\"`\n  - *Status:* **DISCOVERY / EXPLANATION** (Needs direct, clear explanation of `attempts_count`, `created_at` ordering, and how new scans enter the queue).\n- **Auto-Deploy to Surge Rule (Standing Directive):**\n  - *User Directive:* `\"deploy it to surge please...and do so going forward after every new compile\"`\n  - *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION** (Must re-export web bundle and deploy via `npx surge ./dist valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh` after every compilation).\n\n---\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **Domain & Core Workflows:**\n  - Target Company: **ValuTeachers** working with Florida educators on the **Florida Retirement System (FRS)** and **403(b)/457(b)** plans.\n  - Primary KPI: **Appointments Set** (`Appt. Set`) — locking in classroom sit-downs during planning periods.\n  - Live Surge Domain: `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n- **User Directives Verbatim:**\n  - *\"for the power dialer HUD, the screen is extremely crowded....the dispo buttons overlap the dial/call button...whether in standard or landscape mode. the ux/ui should unsure efficient and elegant use on any handheld device.\"*\n  - *\"now the swipe right to dial/swipe left to skip functionality doesn't seem fully functional/implemented. please verify\"*\n  - *\"also, the 'Report Card Needs & Inquiries\" section in the HUD doesn't extend to multiple lines and instead runs off of the screen. please elegantly address this utilizing best practices for ux/ui design\"*\n  - *\"ok...the swipe still does not trigger a dial when swiped right. i only have one test record so i'm not sure if the swipe left to skip is actually working, but swipe right is not. my understanding is that swiping right should trigger the same behavior as if the Dial # button was clicked.\"*\n  - *\"just tested the new build. the swipe functionality still isn't working\"*\n  - *\"does the app automatically keep track of where a user left off in their dialing...for example, if i have 13 leads, and i start calling but have to stop after call 7, does the app pick up on lead 8 when i start it back up?\"*\n  - *\"how does it handle it when new leads are added? does it just append them to the end or does it reset the dial count?\"*\n\n---\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n1. **Resolved `Can't find variable BarChart3` & Full Static Analysis Audit:**\n   - Added `BarChart3` to `lucide-react-native` import list in `src/screens/ListsScreen.tsx`.\n   - Updated `src/types/index.ts` `Lead` interface to allow `null` for nullable database columns.\n   - Updated `src/screens/CadenceSettingsScreen.tsx` channel checks (`sms_only`, `call_and_sms`, `call_only`).\n   - Cleaned optional native dynamic imports in `documentScannerService.ts` and `hapticsService.ts`. Verified `tsc` static check with **0 errors**.\n2. **Fixed Power Dialer HUD Layout & Overlapping Dispositions ([`DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx)):**\n   - Wrapped the entire screen in a responsive `<ScrollView>` with `keyboardShouldPersistTaps=\"handled\"`.\n   - Separated the main Dial Button from the 1-Tap Disposition Dock.\n   - Added full-width Hero `🎯 APPOINTMENT SET` button with distinct visual hierarchy.\n   - Restructured remaining dispositions (`💬 Spoke`, `📞 No Answer`, `✉️ AI SMS`, `📅 Callback`) into a 2x2 grid.\n3. **Fixed Multi-Line Wrapping for Report Card Needs & Inquiries ([`DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx), [`LeadDetailScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx)):**\n   - Replaced fixed single-line chips with a flexible checklist format (`interestsList`, `interestRow`, `interestText`).\n   - Added `flex: 1`, `flexWrap: 'wrap'`, and `lineHeight: 17` so long teacher inquiries wrap cleanly without overflowing the viewport.\n4. **Universal Swipe Gesture Engine ([`DialerHudScreen.tsx`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx), [`telephonyService.ts`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer/src/services/telephonyService.ts)):**\n   - Attached universal touch and mouse event listeners (`onTouchStart`, `onTouchMove`, `onTouchEnd`, `onMouseDown`, `onMouseMove`, `onMouseUp`) to `Animated.View` with `touchAction: 'pan-y'`.\n   - Enabled synchronous execution of `handleDial()` / `advanceNextLead()` on gesture release within the user touch context to avoid browser security blocks on `tel:` protocols.\n   - Upgraded `TelephonyService.makeCall()` to trigger direct `window.location.href = url` on web and `Linking.openURL(url)` on native.\n5. **Compiled & Deployed to Surge:**\n   - Production web bundle live at: `https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Dialing Queue Sorting Mechanism (`LeadsRepository.getDialingQueueForList`):**\n  ```sql\n  SELECT * FROM leads \n  WHERE list_id = ? \n    AND (last_disposition IS NULL OR last_disposition IN ('pending', 'no_answer', 'voicemail'))\n  ORDER BY attempts_count ASC, created_at ASC\n  ```\n- **How New Leads Are Handled In the Database:**\n  - When new leads are scanned/imported, they enter the database with `attempts_count = 0` and `last_disposition = null`.\n  - **Does it reset dial count?** **No.** Existing dialed leads retain their actual history (`attempts_count = 1, 2, 3...`), call logs, notes, and dispositions.\n  - **Where do new leads appear?**\n    - If you are in the middle of a 1st attempt run (calling fresh leads with `attempts_count = 0`), new leads are appended after other untouched leads (`created_at ASC`).\n    - If you have already dialed all existing leads once (`attempts_count = 1`), and you scan 5 new leads (`attempts_count = 0`), the new leads **jump to the front of the queue** ahead of the round 2 retry leads, because `attempts_count = 0 < 1`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n\n### Edited Files\n- `src/types/index.ts`: Updated `Lead` interface to allow `null` for nullable fields.\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Hydration and fallback adjustments.\n- `src/screens/CadenceSettingsScreen.tsx`: Corrected cadence rule channel display logic.\n- `src/services/documentScannerService.ts`: Added dynamic import fallbacks.\n- `src/services/hapticsService.ts`: Added dynamic import fallbacks.\n- `src/services/telephonyService.ts`: Upgraded `makeCall` and `sendSMS` for direct web navigation & native linking.\n- `src/screens/DialerHudScreen.tsx`: Added responsive scroll layout, multi-line inquiry wrapping, universal touch/mouse swipe engine with synchronous dial triggering.\n- `src/screens/LeadDetailScreen.tsx`: Applied multi-line text wrapping for inquiries and custom questions.\n- `dist/index.html`: Entry point referencing latest compiled bundle.\n\n### Viewed Files\n- `src/db/leadsRepository.ts`: Contains `getDialingQueueForList` (lines 208–221) and `updateLeadDisposition` (lines 223–250).\n\n---\n\n## 6.