{"step_index":1505,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T19:23:06Z","content":"**It never resets your dial count.** Existing leads and your historical stats/KPIs are permanently preserved.\n\nHere is how the queue dynamically positions newly added leads:\n\n---\n\n### 🎯 2 Scenarios of How New Leads Are Prioritized\n\nThe Power Dialer prioritizes calls using:\n```sql\nORDER BY attempts_count ASC, created_at ASC\n```\nFresh, never-called leads (`attempts_count = 0`) always take top priority over follow-up calls (`attempts_count ≥ 1`).\n\n---\n\n#### **Scenario 1: You are midway through your list**\n*Example: You had 13 leads. You called 7 (`1 attempt`), leaving 6 uncalled (`0 attempts`). You now scan in 5 new leads.*\n* **What happens:** \n  1. The 6 remaining uncalled leads (Leads 8–13) stay up next.\n  2. The 5 newly scanned leads (`0 attempts`) are appended right after Lead 13.\n  3. You call Leads 8 through 18 in one continuous, seamless first-round flow.\n  4. Only after all 18 leads have received Call #1 does the dialer begin Round 2 for any unanswered contacts.\n\n---\n\n#### **Scenario 2: You completed Round 1 and are working on Round 2 (Follow-ups)**\n*Example: You already called all 13 original leads once (`attempts_count = 1`). You now scan in 5 new leads.*\n* **What happens:**\n  1. The 5 newly scanned leads (`0 attempts`) **jump straight to the front of the queue** because fresh leads are the hottest prospects.\n  2. You dial the 5 new leads for their 1st call.\n  3. Once they are completed, the dialer automatically returns to your Round 2 follow-ups on the original 13 leads.\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Key Takeaway\n- **No data loss or reset:** Existing call counts, timestamps, appointment notes, and dispositions remain intact.\n- **Zero manual sorting needed:** The engine ensures you never call an old lead twice before giving every new lead its first call.","thinking":"**Analyzing Lead Entry**\n\nOkay, I'm focusing on how the lead system behaves when fresh entries arrive. Specifically, existing leads won't lose their dialing history or data. Their attempt count and call logs remain untouched, ensuring all historical data stays intact. KPIs and analytics stay put too, which is very important for data integrity.\n\n\n"}
