{"step_index":1507,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T12:59:11Z","content":"Here are the **4 best architectural strategies** to incorporate legacy/aged lead cards without disrupting your active, high-priority pipeline:\n\n---\n\n### 1. 🏆 Recommended: Multi-Tier Priority Weighting (`Hot` vs. `Legacy`)\n*How it works:*\n- Every lead gets a `priority_tier` property:\n  - **Tier 1 (Fresh / Hot - Default):** New cards scanned this school year.\n  - **Tier 2 (Legacy / Archive):** Older cards from past years or prior campaigns.\n- In the queue ordering:\n  ```sql\n  ORDER BY priority_tier ASC, attempts_count ASC, created_at DESC\n  ```\n- **The Result:** The dialer will **never** surface a Tier 2 legacy lead until every single Tier 1 fresh lead has been dialed. When you snap in legacy cards, you simply toggle a *\"Mark as Legacy / Back-Burner\"* switch on the review screen.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Campaign & List Isolation (Dedicated \"Legacy Vault\" List)\n*How it works:*\n- Instead of placing all cards into the default master bucket, you scan them into a dedicated list named **\"2023–2024 Legacy Vault\"** or **\"Archive Re-activation\"**.\n- In the UI:\n  - You can dial your **Active List** during peak hours (e.g., 3:00 PM – 5:30 PM).\n  - You can switch to your **Legacy List** specifically when you have spare downtime or want to run a dedicated re-engagement blast.\n\n---\n\n### 3. \"Warm Sweep\" / Downtime Calling Filter\n*How it works:*\n- In the Power Dialer launch screen, add a 1-tap **Queue Filter Mode**:\n  - 🟢 **Fresh Inquiries Only** (Never dialed, current season)\n  - 🟡 **Follow-Ups & Callbacks** (Step 2+ multi-touch)\n  - 🟣 **Legacy Sweep** (Aged cards called at the very end of the day or during school breaks)\n- Keeps your master database unified while giving you total control over who you dial in any given session.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Backdated Age Stamp / Artificial Attempt Seeding\n*How it works:*\n- When scanning legacy cards, the system marks their `created_at` with an older date or assigns an initial `priority_score = 99`.\n- Because the queue sorts by freshness and attempt stage, older timestamped records naturally float to the bottom of the stack without needing custom manual sorting.\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Recommendation for ValuTeachers Workflow\nCombining **Strategy 1 (Priority Tier toggle on scan)** with **Strategy 2 (Named Lists)** gives you the cleanest experience:\n1. When snapping old report cards, you toggle **\"Legacy / Low Priority\"** (or assign them to a *\"Legacy Archive\"* list).\n2. Your daily high-value calling periods remain 100% focused on fresh teacher requests.\n3. When fresh leads are exhausted, the app seamlessly dips into the legacy backlog so no potential appointment is left on the table.","thinking":"**Prioritizing Old Leads**\n\nOkay, I'm thinking about these legacy leads. The goal is to integrate them without disrupting the current system. I'm leaning toward appending them to the end of the calling queue. But, that might not be optimal, so I am weighing a strategy to incorporate them by assessing current queue order and appending only based on factors like time since lead creation, or previous unsuccessful contact attempts. I could also add these as a separate queue to be cycled through at a certain cadence, so I'm investigating those strategies.\n\n\n"}
